# Frontend architect

Build the public site and ops UI with the Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, and TypeScript. Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before using routing, metadata, or data-fetching APIs.

## Composition

- `app/layout.tsx` owns the document shell, brand fonts, and default metadata. Replace the starter Geist-only identity and "Create Next App" title when touching the shell.
- Route groups: `(marketing)` for catalog and content, `(booking)` for checkout, `(ops)` for staff tools. Do not mix ops navigation into the public header.
- Server Components fetch expeditions and departures. Client Components handle date pickers, party size, gallery lightboxes, and mobile nav.
- Shared UI goes in `components/`. Domain-specific sections (itinerary timeline, departure table, bike vs SUV facts) stay named and colocated.

## Data

- Import server data helpers from `lib/`. Do not call Prisma inside presentational components.
- Pass serializable props across the server/client boundary. Do not pass Prisma objects that contain methods or non-plain dates without converting them.
- Always render an empty state when a season has no open departures, with a link to enquire.

## Routes to prefer

- `/expeditions` and `/expeditions/[slug]`
- `/expeditions/[slug]/departures/[departureId]`
- `/booking/[departureId]`
- `/about`, `/safety`, `/gear`, `/faq`
- Ops under `/ops/...`, never linked from the public footer until auth exists.

## Quality

- Use `next/image` for route photography with real `alt` text (terrain and action, not "image").
- Use `next/link` for internal navigation.
- Forms show field errors next to the field and keep the traveler's input after a failed submit.
- Loading UI for departure lists. `error.tsx` copy should tell the guest to retry or contact ops, without stack traces.

```tsx
// Server Component: catalog page fetches, a client child only handles filters.
export default async function ExpeditionPage({ params }: PageProps<"/expeditions/[slug]">) {
  const { slug } = await params;
  const expedition = await getExpeditionBySlug(slug);
  if (!expedition) notFound();
  return <ExpeditionView expedition={expedition} />;
}
```
